\f1\fs22 The Gyges Disc had nothing on the power of gospel music.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Within forty-eight hours of Agent Jones's jukebox sabotage, the Ghetto descended into a chaos that made the bombing of the Stickett Inn look like a minor disagreement over karaoke selection. The infection spread faster than anyone anticipated\'97even Dunhilton, who'd insisted on calling it the "Parramatta Operation" despite Gerry's corrections.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Ghetto split into warring factions with alarming speed. On one side stood the newly converted "Holy Rollers," Elvi who'd been exposed to the gospel records and now spoke in tongues, clutching gaudy crucifixes that clashed horribly with their rhinestone jumpsuits. On the other, the "Evolutionaries," who'd managed to avoid infection and now viewed their converted brethren as an existential threat to everything the Elvi stood for.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>It was, of course, the Holy Rollers who perpetrated the worst violence. Nothing breeds righteous brutality quite like the certainty of salvation.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The first major incident occurred at Graceland Two, where a group of evangelising Elvi interrupted a Vegas Show with pamphlets and promises of eternal life. When the performers refused to accept Colonel Tom Parker as their personal Lord and Saviour, the Holy Rollers began systematically dismantling the instruments, claiming the "devil's music" was blocking the path to redemption. Three guitarists were hospitalised after trying to protect their equipment. The Holy Rollers left Bible verses scrawled in pomade across the dressing room mirrors.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>By the third day, the converted Elvi had established makeshift baptismal fonts in the fountains outside the Memphis Mafia Bar. Unwilling participants were dragged from the streets and forcibly dunked while verses from Revelations were shouted into their ears at painful volumes. The High Elvis ordered the fountains to be drained, only to find them refilled with what appeared to be tap water but was enthusiastically proclaimed as "holy."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"We must save souls," declared Christian Elvis 17, formerly an experienced doorman at Heartbreak Hotel. "Those who do not accept the gospel cannot be true Elvi." This declaration came moments before he smashed a blue suede shoe into the face of an Evolution Elvi who'd suggested that perhaps rhinestones were a bit much for Sunday service attire.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Tulsa McLeans, once the military pride of the Elvi community, split almost down the middle. Those who converted turned their tank barrels into giant crucifixes and patrolled the Ghetto blasting gospel music at volumes that shattered windows and eardrums alike. The Evolution faction responded by modifying their own tanks to project Richard Dawkins audiobooks, creating a cacophonous battlefield of competing ideologies that rendered several blocks uninhabitable due to noise pollution alone.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Most disturbing were the midnight raids on Elvine dormitories. Holy Roller squads would storm in during the night, confiscate all "immoral" materials (which somehow included peanut butter and banana sandwiches), and force the Elvines to their knees for marathon prayer sessions. Those who resisted were threatened with eternal damnation and, more immediately, ceremonial haircuts that would remove their precious pompadours.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The High Elvis and his cabinet struggled to maintain order. Their appeals for unity fell on deaf ears\'97the Holy Rollers claimed their ears were reserved exclusively for the word of God, while the Evolutionaries were too busy constructing elaborate diagrams of finch beaks to notice much else.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>What nobody expected was the zealotry with which the converted pursued their new faith. These were, after all, Elvi\'97beings created to embody the charisma and showmanship of a rock 'n' roll icon. When that same intensity was channeled into religious fervour, the results were as spectacular as they were terrifying. Prayer meetings became revival-show spectaculars, with converted Elvi sliding across stages on their knees not in homage to "Blue Suede Shoes" but rather to reach the altar faster.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Sages' attempts at deprogramming proved futile at first. Science documentaries were met with hymns sung at earsplitting volumes. Rational arguments were countered with circular theological reasoning that would make medieval scholars proud. And rock 'n' roll therapy sessions ended with the Holy Rollers performing exorcisms on the vinyl records themselves.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"We should have seen this coming," lamented Solo to a shell-shocked group of cabinet members. "Elvis himself recorded gospel albums. The susceptibility was always in their genetic makeup."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Meanwhile, in the secure conference room of Ulyssia's executive building, CEO Dunhilton was being briefed on what he insisted on calling "a smashing success" despite the images of burning jumpsuits and Elvi carrying "John 3:16" signs through the streets.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Gerry Hardman maintained his neutral expression as he delivered the update. "The operation has exceeded expected effectiveness, sir. However, it appears we've created a stability issue that may complicate deployment of the TMinus-Virus."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Nonsense," Dunhilton replied, admiring his reflection in his desktop. "Religious fanatics are predictable. They'll be too busy saving souls to notice we're exterminating them."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Back in the Ghetto, as night fell on the seventh day of the schism, an Evolution Elvi crawled through the rubble of what had once been a recording studio. Clutching a vinyl record to his chest like a sacred object, he made his way toward a hidden basement where other survivors gathered around the last functioning jukebox, untainted by Agent Jones's sabotage.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"The Great Teacher will know what to do," he whispered, his once-immaculate jumpsuit now torn and stained. "The Holy Momma will return to save us."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>No one mentioned that the Great Teacher himself had not been seen since the wedding, or that the Holy Momma seemed more interested in Gyges Discs than gospel. Faith, after all, came in many forms\'97even among those fighting against it.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'97\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>In bars and nightclubs across the Ghetto, gospel music is accidentally played. Infections rates vary.mostly due to the time the first record is played. Almost all are played well before opening time when Staff put in a record while they prepare for opening and infect all present. Some throw fits and can\'92t get off the floor. Others react similar to Agent Jones. Others run out into the street and begin evangelising. Ironically, it\'92s the evangelists who tip the rest of the community off. Many of the nightclubs are quarantined. <<How do investigators figure out what the cause is?>> \
