\fs14 st
\fs22  Draft\'85\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>A group of five Elvi were lying flat, frothing at the mouth, in an apparent fit, each with ear-phones attached to a prehistoric music device. A small group gathered around them, one Elvis took the earphones from one of the Elvi, still jerking about on the ground and listened. His eyes widened and then threw the teeny speakers to the ground.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Gospel music!!\'94 He yelled and then vomited, stumbling as best he could for the nearest exit. Screams of panic filled the air as Elvi clamoured over each other in urgency and desperation, all heading in any direction away from the reviled tunes. The High Elvis rushed from the stage and stood before them in horror. They were not fitting, not like any epileptic he had ever seen. They were jerking about and talking some absolute gibberish as white foam spilled over their chins and the front of their jackets, running rivers of drool and bubbles between the rhinestones. Every so often, they would simultaneously break out into shouts of \'93Praise be to Jesus! The Lord and Saviour! Pledge now, pledge now.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What has happened to them?\'94 The High Elvis asked\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93They are suffering from an extreme case of Evangelism and we are all susceptible if exposure is protracted. The harmonies of Gospel are just too powerful for an Elvis to resist,\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93conducting white masses, baptising each other and then got into sexual abstinence.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Celibacy? That\'92s just plain sick.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>- - - \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleo, Solo and Chilo sat before the High Elvis and his nervous cabinet in the committee room. They were hopeful of good news from the enlightened ones, but they looked somber and caught no-one in the eye.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93They are all devout, have no sense of humour and follow neither logic nor reason. This infection has blocked their capacity to comprehend simple scientific facts. They are, for want of a better term, possessed by the Jesus and we have no alternative but to excise this meme and purge them of faith.\'94 Kleo had not seen faith manifest itself with such fervour and doubted anything, at least in the short term, was going to work. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93How is that achieved? I do not want them to come to harm.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Of course, High Elvis. I think we should start off by playing rock and roll music, twenty four hours a day. Then science documentaries, interspersed with de-programming sessions where my apprentices and I will challenge their beliefs with rational argument and scientific truth. If this fails we may have to call on ancient methods to rid them of evil.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I authorise you and your apprentices to commence the rock n\'92 roll therapy and the follow up documentary and counselling sessions, wise one.\'94 The High Elvis felt like he was getting used to this leadership thing. \'93I want regular reports. We will reassess as each day goes by.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93___, High Elvis.\'94 Kleo reluctantly admitted. \'93Chilo, Solo and I have been working non-stop for 7 days, but nothing seemed to penetrate the mindlessness of their faith. They cannot seem to ignore the false promise of life ever-lasting, the dishonest certainty of faith.\'94 Each Elvis held fast to their belief, in the face of irresistible logical argument thrown at them by the wise three.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What next, great one.\'94 High Elvis wanted to hear better news, but was hopeful the next round of treatment may work.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I think we have no choice, but to adopt some ancient methods from antiquity.\'94 Kleo was deliberately vague, he did not want to use the word exorcism, because it would not be an entirely accurate description and would not be met with any enthusiasm. \'93Initially, I would suggest we try the new protocols on one Elvis only. If we make errors, it will only affect one Elvis and we can improve as we process them one at a time.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93They are not to be harmed deliberately. My cabinet colleagues and I are most adamant that no harm come to them.\'94 The High Elvis had mentioned his abhorrence to violence being visited upon his precious creed of clones far too many times for Kleo to forget. \'93I am placing my faith in you, great Sages.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Thank you, High Elvis.\'94 Kleo bowed his head slightly. \'93Solo and Chilo, we shall prepare ourselves to fight this insidious Jesus.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93This is a fight for the hearts and minds of all the Elvi, we cannot afford to lose.\'94 Solo followed Kleo out of the President\'92s Office and prepared himself to do battle with evil.\
